A||N||9||Capt Fiero||Building a 2.8||||5||
Z||000000||Capt Fiero||09-18-2000||10:45 PM||||Hey all it has been awhile since I posted here.  I was in the middle of a 3.4 conversion but has since been sold.  I am now doing a Hot Rod 2.8.  I want to get some opnions on what I am doing and what you think that I am going to get out of it.  Any and all input is welcome.  Well here goes.<BR>Fiero HO heads.<BR>Speed Pro Cam.Gross cam lift. .280 @ 208 degrees with .50 lift.  Same for intake and exhaust.  <BR>Injectors are 19# from a mustang<BR>Exhaust is ported manifolds with flowmaster muffler and straight through cat.<BR>Intake is Enlarged throttle body to 55mm, K-n-N Filter remove water seperator, and install a holly side scoop, (I like the look of the scoop even if it does nothing)<BR>Trans is an 86 4spd with the 3.65 FDR.  Stock pistons, stock valves. All I am looking for is 170hp that is only a 30hp gain from the porting and the cam and the larger injectors, oh and MSD blaster coil ignition.  The engine is being gone through from top to bottom new bearings, in con rods and crank, the crank has been taken to a machine shop and had it polished to a real shine.  I am looking for a 14.5 in the quarter with it.  I know that to go faster than that I will need at least a 50hp nos shot at least.  The car is a combination of<BR>85GT with 88GT Guages and Aux Guage pod, 88GT lace Wheels, and a ton of other odds and ends that I have grabbed from other parts cars.  I have pics of the car up at photo point with the rear sway bar install. I will post those in a second.  The car at last weight was 2750lbs without driver.  that was with the auto trans I think that the 4spd is about 70lbs lighter.  Any Input from fiero hot rod engine people please let me know any tricks of the field.<BR>David <P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>www.westcoastfieros.com||||reg||5
Z||000001||Capt Fiero||09-18-2000||11:04 PM||||The link to the photopoint page is <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1006279&Auth=false" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1006279&Auth=false</A>   I hope that it works if not just go to <A HREF="http://www.photopoint.com" TARGET=_blank>www.photopoint.com</A>  and go enter in my email address captfieroofbc@home.com look in capts cars to see what I am working with and pics of the rear sway bar install.<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>www.westcoastfieros.com||||reg||6
Z||000002||80's BOY||09-19-2000||10:11 AM||||i just installed a set of Mustang injectors on my 3.1 stroker and they were WAY too much for it. you may have problems there. i spent a whole day tuning the fuel pressures to make it work and it would not. that may be the first problem upon initial startup. i put the 2.8 injectors back in.||||reg||5
Z||000003||GT Bastard||09-19-2000||10:33 AM||||Just out of curiosity, why not a 3.1?  It's very little extra money.  1FST2M6 was able to pull a best of 14.7 in the quarter with my car, but that's with a full race-clutch, extrude honed intake, 2.5 flomaster exhaust, tweaked fuel delivery, different prom, ported exhaust manifolds(now headers), sticky Yoko tires, MSD ignition, SI valves w/ stiffer springs, weight reduction, etc...  And this is after plenty of chassis dyno tuning.  I would probably expect mid 15's with the combo you mentioned.  A lot of 4sp guys seem to be running 15's and 16's even with a 3.1  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||09-19-2000||12:51 PM||||your gunna need perfect fuel mapping and ignition mapping to make that tiny motor pull 14.5... i've logged hours on the dyno tweaking chips, and timing, fuel, exhaust... air pressure on the body @ speed... and once all that was said an done it was not a very civilized ride. fast as all get up but not a daily driver.. (you think so GT Bastard?) you can do it and you'll surley be impressed with it but you'll get tired of the fuel consumption pretty quick. the easyest way to go is nitrous... with no real mod you'll pull 14.5 all day.. and never have motor problems or lack of fuel issues. nos part #05120, <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nosnitrous.com</A>  or NX # 13093 <A HREF="http://www.nitrousexpress.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrousexpress.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Capt Fiero||09-19-2000||03:33 PM||||80's boy, which mustang injectors did you use.  Mustang had 19,24,30 and on up.  I was thinking that stock 15# would not give me enough at 6000rpms with the new cam.  That is why I am jumping to 19#.  I guess I am going to be looking for 15 flat in the quarter not 14.5.  Oh well lets just see what happens<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||80's BOY||09-19-2000||04:25 PM||||i used 19# ones.(they are for sale $25 and i'll send them to ya) my next guess would be 305 GM TPI injectors if it were me. i don't feel like pulling the rail and plenum two more times to try though.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||09-19-2000||08:40 PM||||80's boy, thank you for conferming my theory. I'm just waiting on the machine shop for my 3.1 back, and unfortunatly I don't have the cash to go investing in new injectors and what not. but from what I could tell the stock injectors ran rich in the 2.8, so if I could suck in a bit more air, they should be pretty close to right on. altho, there is one thing I've been wondering about with everyone running adjustable fuel preasure. GM designed those injectors to create a specific spray arch for optimal fuel/air mixture. wouldn't anything more then minor tweaking cause more problems then good? expecially when you change to different injectors all together. I dunno, just a thought||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||09-20-2000||09:08 PM||||Your car will run about a 14.8 @ 90 MPH and have about 160 HP.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Capt Fiero||09-20-2000||09:13 PM||||I will be happy with that.  Then maybe a 50hp NOS shot. LOL.  ||||reg||1
